{"chapter": "criteria", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "05Y8", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathit{Mor}_B(Z, X)$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathit{Mor}_B(Z, Z)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{proposition-hom-functor-algebraic-space}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-fibre-diagram}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{spaces-lemma-fibre-product-spaces-over-sheaf-with-representable-diagonal}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1b25ff1169228512375677c362c3af156c29ebd04736490947988045a3769ab5", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:eaf23400885082abc887fb13e923681972e61b954b7f5901016a52212de6b11d", "source_text": "By\nProposition <REF_0001>\nthe functors <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002>\nare algebraic spaces. Hence this follows from the cartesian\ndiagram of\nLemma <REF_0002>\nand the fact that fibre products of algebraic spaces exist and\nare given by the fibre product in the underlying category of\nsheaves of sets (see\nSpaces, Lemma\n<REF_0003>).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c055ad47bb675dcf7edf68bb3ba977ffe834333594bbf6dc6a17f80e1eac97e8", "unit_id": "tag:05YF:proof"}
